WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.860
Speaker 1: We have to start today with Russia
and Ukraine, where there are both reasons

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:11.080
to be absolutely horrified about what may
be coming to the planet over the next several

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:14.110
weeks, but also some reasons to be cautiously
optimistic.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:18.160
And we're going to talk about both and we
should understand both.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:26.020
On the one hand, the bad we are facing what
Kamala Harris calls a real possibility of

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:33.100
what Boris Johnson refers to as the biggest
European war since World War Two.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:40.290
We have no reason to believe at this point
that Russia and Putin were telling the truth

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.219
about pulling back.

00:00:42.219 --> 00:00:46.469
There has not been any independently verified
evidence that suggests that's what's taking

00:00:46.469 --> 00:00:48.910
place despite the claims last week.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:54.030
And there is reason to believe, according
to President Joe Biden, that Vladimir Putin

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:58.280
has already made the decision to invade Ukraine.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:07.969
Now, I don't know if we need to refresh the
entire situation, but Russia points to so-called

00:01:07.969 --> 00:01:15.539
NATO's expansion and support of Ukraine from
Naito as an act of aggression.

00:01:15.539 --> 00:01:23.609
The actual aggressor in the case of Russia
and Ukraine is clearly Putin.

00:01:23.609 --> 00:01:28.650
But there are some who say his aggression
is justified, and this includes, I mean, in

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:33.990
the U.S., some on the right and some on the
left for different reasons, many of them victims

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:36.899
of different types of propaganda, which we
will talk about.

00:01:36.899 --> 00:01:41.299
But let's go to some of what world leaders
are saying, and it doesn't really matter whether

00:01:41.299 --> 00:01:42.599
you like these world leaders.

00:01:42.599 --> 00:01:45.739
I don't particularly love either of them.

00:01:45.739 --> 00:01:48.700
But let's talk about what is being said.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:53.289
Here is a British Prime Minister Boris Johnson.

00:01:53.289 --> 00:01:54.289
Take a listen.

00:01:54.289 --> 00:01:59.049
Speaker 2: The plan that we're seeing is for
something that could be really the biggest

00:01:59.049 --> 00:02:03.509
war in Europe since 1945 in just in terms
